\section{Introduction}
PROJECT G.A.L.A.C.T.I.C. is a multi-layer gravitational anomaly detection
and antigravity coupling stability engine. It integrates astrophysical
tensor fields, Hamiltonian dynamics, structural tensegrity analysis, and
timeline-based regime classification.

This manual provides a complete technical description of the system,
including mathematical foundations, simulation workflow, structural
analysis, and laboratory execution guidelines.

%------------------------------------------------------------
\section{System Overview}
The system is divided into four operational layers:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item Astrophysical Intake and Tensor Validation
    \item Hamiltonian Dynamics and Coupling Core
    \item Structural Geometry and Tensegrity Analysis
    \item Event-Drift Timeline Classification
\end{enumerate}

Each layer is modular and can be executed independently or as part of the
full simulation pipeline.

%------------------------------------------------------------
\section{Astrophysical Intake Layer}
\subsection{Input Data}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Stellar kinematics (GAIA-like)
    \item CMB anisotropy tensor fields
    \item Quasar drift time-series
    \item Cosmic ray flux
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Tensor Validation}
The intake layer performs:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Field consistency checks
    \item Tensor alignment verification
    \item Statistical validity analysis
\end{itemize}

The output is a validated tensor field $T_{\mu\nu}(x)$ and initial
conditions for particle states.

